   1:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c **** /**
   2:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   ******************************************************************************
   3:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   * @file    stm32f4xx_sdio.c
   4:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   * @author  MCD Application Team
   5:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   * @version V1.8.0
   6:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   * @date    04-November-2016
   7:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   * @brief   This file provides firmware functions to manage the following 
   8:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   *          functionalities of the Secure digital input/output interface (SDIO) 
   9:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   *          peripheral:
  10:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   *           + Initialization and Configuration
  11:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   *           + Command path state machine (CPSM) management
  12:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   *           + Data path state machine (DPSM) management
  13:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   *           + SDIO IO Cards mode management
  14:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   *           + CE-ATA mode management
  15:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   *           + DMA transfers management
  16:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   *           + Interrupts and flags management
  17:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   *
  18:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c **** @verbatim
  19:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c **** 
  20:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****  ===================================================================
  21:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****                  ##### How to use this driver #####
  22:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****  ===================================================================
  23:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****  [..]
  24:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****    (#) The SDIO clock (SDIOCLK = 48 MHz) is coming from a specific output of PLL 
  25:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (PLL48CLK). Before to start working with SDIO peripheral make sure that the
  26:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        PLL is well configured.
  27:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        The SDIO peripheral uses two clock signals:
  28:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) SDIO adapter clock (SDIOCLK = 48 MHz)
  29:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) APB2 bus clock (PCLK2)
  30:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        
ARM GAS  /tmp/cceMuoz3.s 			page 2


  31:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        -@@- PCLK2 and SDIO_CK clock frequencies must respect the following condition:
  32:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****            Frequency(PCLK2) >= (3 / 8 x Frequency(SDIO_CK))
  33:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   
  34:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****    (#) Enable peripheral clock using RCC_APB2PeriphClockCmd(RCC_APB2Periph_SDIO, ENABLE).
  35:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   
  36:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****    (#) According to the SDIO mode, enable the GPIO clocks using 
  37:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        RCC_AHB1PeriphClockCmd() function. 
  38:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        The I/O can be one of the following configurations:
  39:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) 1-bit data length: SDIO_CMD, SDIO_CK and D0.
  40:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) 4-bit data length: SDIO_CMD, SDIO_CK and D[3:0].
  41:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) 8-bit data length: SDIO_CMD, SDIO_CK and D[7:0].      
  42:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   
  43:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****    (#) Peripheral alternate function: 
  44:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) Connect the pin to the desired peripherals' Alternate Function (AF) 
  45:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****            using GPIO_PinAFConfig() function
  46:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) Configure the desired pin in alternate function by: 
  47:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****            GPIO_InitStruct->GPIO_Mode = GPIO_Mode_AF
  48:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) Select the type, pull-up/pull-down and output speed via GPIO_PuPd, 
  49:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****            GPIO_OType and GPIO_Speed members
  50:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) Call GPIO_Init() function
  51:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   
  52:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****    (#) Program the Clock Edge, Clock Bypass, Clock Power Save, Bus Wide, 
  53:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        hardware, flow control and the Clock Divider using the SDIO_Init()
  54:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        function.
  55:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   
  56:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****    (#) Enable the Power ON State using the SDIO_SetPowerState(SDIO_PowerState_ON) 
  57:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        function.
  58:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****                 
  59:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****    (#) Enable the clock using the SDIO_ClockCmd() function.
  60:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   
  61:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****    (#) Enable the NVIC and the corresponding interrupt using the function 
  62:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        SDIO_ITConfig() if you need to use interrupt mode. 
  63:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   
  64:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****    (#) When using the DMA mode 
  65:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) Configure the DMA using DMA_Init() function
  66:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) Active the needed channel Request using SDIO_DMACmd() function
  67:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   
  68:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****    (#) Enable the DMA using the DMA_Cmd() function, when using DMA mode. 
  69:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   
  70:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****    (#) To control the CPSM (Command Path State Machine) and send 
  71:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        commands to the card use the SDIO_SendCommand(), 
  72:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        SDIO_GetCommandResponse() and SDIO_GetResponse() functions. First, user has
  73:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        to fill the command structure (pointer to SDIO_CmdInitTypeDef) according 
  74:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        to the selected command to be sent.
  75:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        The parameters that should be filled are:
  76:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) Command Argument
  77:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) Command Index
  78:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) Command Response type
  79:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) Command Wait
  80:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) CPSM Status (Enable or Disable).
  81:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   
  82:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        -@@- To check if the command is well received, read the SDIO_CMDRESP
  83:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****            register using the SDIO_GetCommandResponse().
  84:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****            The SDIO responses registers (SDIO_RESP1 to SDIO_RESP2), use the
  85:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****            SDIO_GetResponse() function.
  86:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   
  87:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****    (#) To control the DPSM (Data Path State Machine) and send/receive 
ARM GAS  /tmp/cceMuoz3.s 			page 3


  88:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        data to/from the card use the SDIO_DataConfig(), SDIO_GetDataCounter(), 
  89:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        SDIO_ReadData(), SDIO_WriteData() and SDIO_GetFIFOCount() functions.
  90:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   
  91:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****  *** Read Operations ***
  92:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****  =======================
  93:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****  [..]
  94:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****    (#) First, user has to fill the data structure (pointer to
  95:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        SDIO_DataInitTypeDef) according to the selected data type to be received.
  96:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        The parameters that should be filled are:
  97:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) Data TimeOut
  98:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) Data Length
  99:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) Data Block size
 100:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) Data Transfer direction: should be from card (To SDIO)
 101:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) Data Transfer mode
 102:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) DPSM Status (Enable or Disable)
 103:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****                                      
 104:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****    (#) Configure the SDIO resources to receive the data from the card
 105:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        according to selected transfer mode (Refer to Step 8, 9 and 10).
 106:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   
 107:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****    (#)  Send the selected Read command (refer to step 11).
 108:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****                     
 109:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****    (#) Use the SDIO flags/interrupts to check the transfer status.
 110:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   
 111:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****  *** Write Operations ***
 112:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****  ========================
 113:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****  [..]
 114:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****    (#) First, user has to fill the data structure (pointer to
 115:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        SDIO_DataInitTypeDef) according to the selected data type to be received.
 116:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        The parameters that should be filled are:
 117:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) Data TimeOut
 118:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) Data Length
 119:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) Data Block size
 120:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) Data Transfer direction:  should be to card (To CARD)
 121:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) Data Transfer mode
 122:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        (++) DPSM Status (Enable or Disable)
 123:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   
 124:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****    (#) Configure the SDIO resources to send the data to the card according to 
 125:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****        selected transfer mode (Refer to Step 8, 9 and 10).
 126:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****                      
 127:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****    (#) Send the selected Write command (refer to step 11).
 128:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****                     
 129:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****    (#) Use the SDIO flags/interrupts to check the transfer status.
 130:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   
 131:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c ****   
 132:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_sdio.c **** @endverbatim
